==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmædʒɪstɹeɪt/|/ˈmædʒɪstɹət/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-magistrate.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Etymology===

From Latin ''magistratus''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|legal}} A [[judicial]] [[officer]] with limited authority to administer and enforce the [[law]]. A magistrate's court may have jurisdiction in [[civil]] or [[criminal]] cases, or both.
# {{label|en|historical}}  A high official of the state or a municipality in ancient Greece or Rome.
# {{label|en|historical|by extension}} A comparable official in medieval or modern institutions.
# {{label|en|Quebec}} A [[master's degree]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|judicial officer}} {{l|en|justiciary}}
* {{sense|master's degree}} ''See'' '''[[master's degree]]'''

